Source: kvlite
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: KVLite packagers <packages@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), golang-go (>= 1.23), ca-certificates
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/webong/KVlite
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: kvlite-leveldb
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite engine-neutral key-value store (LevelDB driver)
 KVLite core with the pure-Go LevelDB storage driver, installed as a
 versioned, checksummed module catalog plus an extension-free host CLI.
 .
 Set KVLITE_SYSTEM_MODULE_PATH=/usr/lib/kvlite (installed by default in
 /etc/profile.d/kvlite.sh) and run `kvlite serve` or `kvlite module list`.

Package: kvlite-http
Architecture: any
Depends: kvlite-leveldb | kvlite-rocksdb, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite standalone JSON/HTTP protocol module
 The kvlite-http executable module: a direct owner or an HTTP owner for
 attached Redis processes. Needs one installed kvlite driver package.

Package: kvlite-redis
Architecture: any
Depends: kvlite-leveldb | kvlite-rocksdb, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite standalone Redis-compatible protocol module
 The kvlite-redis executable module: a direct owner or an attached process
 over an HTTP owner. Needs one installed kvlite driver package.

# Uncomment for distros whose RocksDB development packages you have pinned;
# set the dependency to your release's library name, e.g.
#   apt-cache search '^librocksdb'
# on Debian/Ubuntu. The bundle links the system engine dynamically and
# verifies it at install time; prefer a --bundle-runtime build wherever the
# system library cannot be pinned (see packaging/README.md).
